The prescribed Granite run exposes a baseline limitation: on this ARM host, `-cmoe` still permits `CPU_REPACK` buffers, so fill reports “expert tensors not mmap-backed” and stays inactive. P12 can still trace the host selections.

I’ll retain the exact off/on checks and add active-path checks using the existing `LLAMA_ARG_REPACK=0` setting. That will exercise mapped fill, pinning, and temporal prediction without changing the loader or the requested command.
